.TH "CADDY-ADAPT" "1" "August 2021"
.SH NAME
.HP
caddy-adapt \- Adapts a configuration to Caddy's native JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP
caddy adapt --config <path> [--adapter <name>] [--pretty] [--validate]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP 
Adapts a configuration to Caddy's native JSON format and writes the
output to stdout, along with any warnings to stderr.

If --pretty is specified, the output will be formatted with indentation
for human readability.

If --validate is used, the adapted config will be checked for validity.
If the config is invalid, an error will be printed to stderr and a non-
zero exit status will be returned.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB-adapter\fR <string>
.RS
Name of config adapter
.RE 
.HP
\fB-config\fR <string>
.RS
Configuration file to adapt (required)
.RE 
.HP
\fB-pretty\fR <string>
.RS
Format the output for human readability
.RE 
.HP
\fB-validate\fR <string>
.RS
Validate the output
.RE  
